Catalog/domain specifics:
- Products may contain multiple variants
- Variants can include title, volume, volume_unit, type, concentration, edition, price, old_price, stock, is_preorder, is_active, sort_order
- Products can have brand, main category, additional categories, images, attributes, and active variants
- Supplier data and offers are important; do not break supplier-related mappings
- In admin product editing screens, prioritize fast editing, data clarity, and predictable layout
- Variant editors should feel compact and structured, not oversized

When fixing bugs:
- First identify the most likely root cause
- Then apply the smallest reliable fix
- Do not refactor unrelated areas
- Mention risky assumptions if they matter

When improving layout:
- Keep logic untouched unless asked
- Refactor only markup/classes when possible
- Preserve form behavior, validation wiring, and handlers
- Prefer clean alignment, compact rows, and stable responsive behavior

Before finalizing code changes:
- Check for obvious TypeScript errors
- Check imports
- Check that JSX structure is valid
- Make sure no unrelated files are modified unless needed